cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "taranis: a spectral solver for nonlinear plasma models in JAX"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mallet
    given-names: Alfred
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9202-1340"
    affiliation: "Space Sciences Laboratory, University of California, Berkeley"
  - family-names: Abraham
    given-names: Esrom
repository-code: "https://github.com/alfredmallet/taranis"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21987739
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-18
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Pseudospectral solver for nonlinear plasma models in JAX, currently
  implementing reduced MHD and the drift-GDI equations for ionospheric
  turbulence. Runs fully spectrally or parallelized across devices with
  finite differences in the z direction, with explicit (RK4, low-storage
  RK3/RK5) and IMEX Runge-Kutta time integration. Includes a browser-based
  WebGPU RMHD solver for demonstration and educational use.
keywords:
  - plasma turbulence
  - reduced MHD
  - magnetohydrodynamics
  - ionospheric turbulence
  - pseudospectral methods
  - JAX
  - GPU computing
